From 5b32d8427476f50f62c8cfd72d9f25e76ea0aadf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 16:37:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix cross-event QR scan security hole; fix inline QR image in
 emails

- db.js/server.js: /api/verify was looking up scan tokens globally across
  ALL events with no check that the token belonged to the event currently
  being scanned for. A QR issued for Event A would verify as valid at Event
  B's gate for any scanning staff member who also had access to Event A -
  which every admin always does by default. Now /api/verify is event-scoped
  like every other route (requireEventRole('scanner') + x-event-id), and
  verifyTxn() rejects a token whose event_id doesn't match with a new
  'wrong-event' result instead of silently verifying it.
- index.html: send x-event-id on the verify call (previously omitted), and
  show a distinct 'Wrong event' message for the new result instead of
  lumping it in with plain 'Invalid pass'.
- mailer.js/server.js: the inline QR in confirmation emails was a base64
  data: URI, which many mail clients (Gmail, Outlook, corporate filters)
  silently strip - so it rendered as nothing even though the HTML was
  valid. Replaced with a real hosted image URL: added a public GET
  /api/qr/:token route (safe to expose unauthenticated - the QR only ever
  encodes the random pass token itself, never personal data, same as the
  existing security model) and pointed the email's <img> at it. The PNG
  attachment stays as an offline fallback. Also added app.set('trust
  proxy', true) so the generated URL correctly resolves to https:// behind
  Railway's reverse proxy.
---
 db.js             |  7 ++++++-
 mailer.js         | 34 +++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 public/index.html |  6 +++++-
 server.js         | 50 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 4 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

